# Scoped Windows long-path artifact-read review

**PASS.** No concrete findings in the single-file unstaged fix. Spec and quality pass for this bounded change.

Reviewed only `git diff -- core/pit_optimizer_v5/artifacts.py` and surrounding source needed to trace the changed operations. Source SHA-256 independently matches `596f5815a9af4f58abeffc730a5793f33072c40bb6914169ca44f6227d7372f3`.

- `_read_relative` now consistently uses extended Windows paths for pre-open metadata, the actual read descriptor and post-read metadata. It retains the pinned parent, reparse rejection, regular-file/single-link checks, identity comparisons, bounded reads and existing exception translation. This addresses the reported mismatch between successful extended-path creation and subsequent plain-path reading of the same existing authority.
- Raw campaign-edge streaming applies the same conversion at its OS boundaries while preserving identity, size, time, link-count and exact digest checks.
- Both lock acquisition paths convert their metadata/open calls without changing lock names, lock byte range, ownership checks, locking behavior or release logic.
- Directory listing and missing-parent diagnosis use extended spelling only for Windows OS calls. Relocation scanning builds returned relative references from unchanged entry names; recursive `DirEntry.path` values may already contain the prefix, which the previously reviewed helper preserves without double-prefixing. Reparse entries remain excluded.
- Repository roots, root identity hashes, artifact references, canonical payloads and saved state identities are unchanged. The patch neither relocates the repository nor resets/removes existing starts; it enables the existing recovery code to read them. POSIX branches receive the original path values and preserve descriptor-relative reads and metadata checks.

This verdict binds to the identified unstaged bytes, not a commit or completed resume. The actual existing 260-character file and its successful independent digest check are controller-reported evidence; they were not opened or re-executed in this source review. Actual recovery remains controller-owned.

No tests were read, written or run. No probes, application imports/execution, Docker, network, agents, commits, staging or hook changes occurred. Only this report was written.
